   </document-link>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2  Indicator 2</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Expanded provision of inclusive market-oriented training 
Indicator: By 2018, 600 students (at least 15% of whom are women and 20% are from excluded groups) enroll in mid-level skills training in market-demanded occupations (Baseline: 11% of enrolled students in sample CTEVT programs in 2012 are women) 
Progress/Status: All 15 mid- level courses have started in all 11 schools with and enrollment capacity of 602. To date 1291 have enrolled in the first year with female percentage of 33% and 55% from excluded groups. The first batch of graduates that were enrolled in 2014 and 2015 were graduated. The data reveals that the first batch of students that were enrolled in 2014 were 40 with only 22 successfully graduating the course. 
Data Source: CTEVT TMIS 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2012"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2018-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2018-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="600"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Expanded provision of inclusive market-oriented training 
Indicator: By 2018, at least 45,000 young people (40% of whom are women 30% are from excluded groups, and 80% are trained by private training providers) complete basic skills training in market-demanded occupations (2012 baseline: 32% of trainees were women and 26% were Dalits) 
Progress/Status: i. 47,500 places have been contracted for training. Out of which, 47,284 (99.55%) have been enrolled in the training with 19,352 (41%) female and 34,047 (72%) disadvantaged candidates.



ii. Total 46,979 out of which 19,289 (41%) female and 33,919 (72%) from disadvantaged group have completed training in Level 1 and Level 2 delivered by public and private TESPs in Round 1 and Round 2.


iii. A total of 46,151 (98.3%) training graduates appeared in skills test. Out of them, skills test results was published for 45,638 (98.9%) and 34,386 (75.4%) training graduates passed the skill test. 
Data Source: CTEVT TMIS 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2012"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2018-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2018-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="45000"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3  Indicator 3</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Improved quality and relevance of TVET provision 
Indicator: By 2017, 15 new or updated mid-level skills training programs in market-demanded occupations introduced in the 10 QIP participating providers 
Progress/Status: 15 new programs (602student capacity) selected for CTEVT constituent Schools. Program curricula developed with total enrollment of 1291 (female-426 &amp; male-851) by June 2018. 
Data Source: CTEVT Accreditation Records 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2012"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2017-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2017-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="15"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3  Indicator 4</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Improved quality and relevance of TVET provision 
Indicator: By 2018, 300 TVET professionals (at least 15% of whom are women and 15% are from excluded groups) have completed training in GESI-sensitive occupational and instructional skills upgrading, curriculum development, and management (2012 baseline: 11% of TVET professionals are women and 4% are Dalits) 
Progress/Status: i. ESI sensitive Human Resource Development (HRD) plan for short term courses prepared and training started in TITI (Contract signed on April 30, 2015).
ii. Twenty-six (26) staff of CTEVT joined for M. Tech and B. Tech programs (3 female); 1 dropped out of the program. 
iii. 582 [102 female (17.5%) and 202 excluded group (34.7%)] (Table 30) CTEVT instructors and staff participated in the GESI sensitive short-term professional development training.  26 TVET professionals enrolled in B.Tech and M.Tech programs.
iv. Total 53 TVET professionals participated in Study Tours to Sri Lanka, Philippines, Hong Kong and Australia. 
Data Source: TITI Training Records 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2012"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2018-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2018-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="300"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Improved quality and relevance of TVET provision 
Indicator: By 2018, at least 10 public providers complete QIP and demonstrate improvement against key indicators, including GESI indicators (Baseline: no public providers have QIP) 
Progress/Status: i. 10 CTEVT constituent schools designated to be developed as model schools and self-assessment completed on September 2014. Activities with quality standards are agreed for the year 2015, 2016, 2017 and 2018.

ii. Four annual progress audits (2015, 2016, 2017 and 2018) were conducted to measure and evaluate progress in the development and implementation of each school&amp;apos;s QIP plan and recommends measures for advancing the implementation of the plan. The audits show that schools are working on the implementation of the QIP and the schools have shown improvement compared to the previous year.

(iii) QIP schools are supported for facility renovation and provided with  tools/equipment to conduct mid level courses. 
Data Source: CTEVT Annual Report 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
